---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Martin Sparks is a software engineering manager based in Scotland, with a background in full-stack engineering and a habit of running long distances."
>

  <!-- Header — dark -->
  <section style="background-color: var(--color-bg-dark);">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 py-20">
      <p class="eyebrow mb-4" style="color: var(--color-muted-on-dark);">About me</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-extrabold mb-6 max-w-2xl leading-tight" style="color: var(--color-text-on-dark);">
        Engineering manager.<br />Runner. Guitarist.
      </h1>
      <p class="text-base leading-relaxed max-w-xl" style="color: var(--color-muted-on-dark);">
        Based in Scotland. Working in software for over a decade.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Bio -->
  <section class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-2xl">
      <p class="eyebrow mb-3">Background</p>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Hi — I'm Martin. I'm a software engineering manager at
          <a href="https://www.insights.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Insights</a>,
          where I lead a multi-disciplinary team of engineers, QA, and design. My background is in
          full-stack engineering — React, TypeScript, Node.js, PostgreSQL — and I try to keep
          enough technical depth to be genuinely useful to the people I work with.
        </p>
        <p>
          The path here wasn't entirely linear. I came to software through
          <a href="https://codeclan.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CodeClan</a>,
          an intensive 16-week bootcamp in Edinburgh, after a stint in technical delivery management
          for the Scottish Government — specifically delivering a £1 million telephony platform into
          Registers of Scotland. Managing suppliers, stakeholders, and the particular chaos of making
          technology work inside a public body turned out to be good preparation for engineering leadership.
        </p>
        <p>
          At Insights I lead a team of ten and own the technical roadmap. The past year has meant a
          large-scale migration off a legacy platform, establishing a community of practice, and building
          the kind of agile culture where people actually want to show up to retrospectives.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Outside work — subtle bg -->
  <section style="background-color: var(--color-bg-subtle);">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
      <p class="eyebrow mb-8">Outside of work</p>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        {[
          {
            title: 'Running',
            body: 'I run regularly and have done for years — long distances, early mornings, often in the dark. It\'s the best way I\'ve found to stay fit and clear my head in equal measure.',
          },
          {
            title: 'Guitar',
            body: 'I\'ve played guitar for over 20 years. Not professionally, not particularly ambitiously — just for the pleasure of it. One of those things that never gets old.',
          },
          {
            title: 'Snowboarding',
            body: 'When there\'s snow, I snowboard. When there isn\'t, I look at weather forecasts and wait.',
          },
        ].map(({ title, body }) => (
          <div
            class="rounded-2xl p-6"
            style="background-color: var(--color-bg); border: 1px solid var(--color-border);"
          >
            <p class="font-bold text-base mb-3" style="color: var(--color-text);">{title}</p>
            <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--color-muted);">{body}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Side project -->
  <section class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-2xl">
      <p class="eyebrow mb-3">Current side project</p>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          I'm building a jigsaw puzzle game — Phaser 3, TypeScript, targeting iOS and Android via
          Capacitor. It's a more interesting technical problem than it sounds: smooth drag physics,
          magnetic snap, piece grouping, and getting 60fps on a five-year-old phone. I'll be writing
          about it here as it takes shape.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Get in touch — dark -->
  <section style="background-color: var(--color-bg-dark);">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
      <p class="eyebrow mb-4" style="color: var(--color-muted-on-dark);">Get in touch</p>
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-6 max-w-md leading-tight" style="color: var(--color-text-on-dark);">
        Always happy to talk.
      </h2>
      <p class="text-base mb-8 max-w-lg" style="color: var(--color-muted-on-dark);">
        Email is the best way to reach me. I'm also on LinkedIn and Strava if those are more your speed.
        There's an RSS feed for the blog too.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a href="mailto:martin.sparks82@gmail.com" class="btn-primary-on-dark">
          Send me an email
        </a>
        <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/martin-sparks" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn-ghost-on-dark">
          LinkedIn
        </a>
        <a href="https://www.strava.com/athletes/97483812" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn-ghost-on-dark">
          Strava
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>
